The camera the person chose as the default camera is the default camera of Qt programs (ORDER 582, patch 0049). QMediaDevices::defaultVideoInput(), a QML MediaDevices and a QCamera made without a device took the first camera of the kernel's list as the default, whatever the person had chosen on the edition's Camera page (WirePlumber's default.configured.video.source). The V4L2 camera backend now follows that key and the session's camera nodes through a PipeWire connection of its own (QtPipeWire::QDefaultCameraMonitor) and marks the camera whose /dev/videoN is the chosen node's api.v4l2.path as the default; every camera stays listed in the same order, a camera a program chooses itself is never touched, and videoInputsChanged is emitted when the choice changes while the program runs. When the chosen camera cannot be found among the cameras (no PipeWire session, the camera unplugged, a camera that is not a V4L2 device) the first camera stays the default as before and the reason is logged once (qt.multimedia.ffmpeg.v4l2cameradevices). tst_qpipewiredefaultcamera covers the choice, the pick, every reason and the monitor without a session.
